From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:30:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 35/37] function runner: prune inconsistent partial insert
 mappings

Paired mutations allocate independent document IDs. Batches of scheduled jobs can have identical metadata shapes while their distinct argument records determine the only valid identity relation. Waiting until a complete assignment to check those references explores irrelevant permutations and exhausts the bounded search even for eight equivalent jobs.

Check every assigned insert against the partial relation before descending. Keep unassigned identities as placeholders, retain the existing search bound, and require the complete write, read and result comparison before accepting a relation. This changes search pruning, not semantic equivalence.

Add a reversed-allocation scheduler-batch regression that reproduced unresolved identity and read/write mismatches before the fix. Verify that changed arguments are still rejected. Make the test read-set builder retain all inserted-ID dependencies within each table instead of overwriting earlier ones.

Validation: all 41 query-shadow comparator tests pass, including cyclic scheduled-operation references, symmetric inserts, partial-search bounds and negative semantic comparisons.
